<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:13:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e8f7fff59c24fec2c7c181e3d76a2fc4e2499e8f94dfa7c925c830facd5695f</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary toughens stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:771476db4ea45a1e8ef3eeaa0ad1834d149cbbf6a1d4af2fe9d30642c54523d4</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:13:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--a42f60a005da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Hungary has expelled 10 Russian diplomats. The Kremlin is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Goethe-Institut is closing in Russia. Russians tell DW how canceled exams are upending their plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3c6f530add9c4d256a3ff3f84d8dac74d056e4f5f4a195c79b60e79a19947dd</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-thei/a-79218936--791b0bcb39e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-their-plans/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia affects their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are electric cars really bad for the environment?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cc20c05363a76c1c78c4cf95630604a58d8d477d05b3d86eba56b6d7415d513</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336--69d71b67dca0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some German politicians are calling for a delay to the EU plan to phase out gas-powered vehicles, saying cars must be judged on the entire carbon footprint. But the full picture still says EVs are more climate friendly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34e5679f071c6fcb4852b2cd9814d7fa529f160df8c7d61f3493d8be768913ce</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:756479a26b6c73a733e641a3ac184f304ecd1b06e76bf3aae0e5a1ab584a3c40</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a37f24238f57f69a8eefa6cb4f340094cd4040fabccc2beb83496bfef65b6515</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic’s funeral casts shadow over Bosnia and Herzegovina vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec5779913b3e2de31c5a04d7e30a6cb9f8d95efc6749153ba37e6e05d5e3b299</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319--342fd5cbe6c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic’s funeral in Belgrade, attended by Serbian and Bosnian Serb leaders, has deepened regional tensions and could affect the upcoming election in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5094e54af2c932f03aa5ec2821e26cb82f36968f4de17bbf8fdfb2dc859b6b8</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c75321766d0865905b5b3f7ab86bf365dff03a14cde941be3a1272a37901ff56</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f03a1883d49f4f4efdfc0e7d0745215c8e2c36244eaf59a6d98ee08c91bbbdf0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62b33af09f6fa50ff326e7fff0b8f436220a0a69c540c0a6a0699e05f268e78a</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3176326cc64c30d549c7b48d74a03a6364182051cd2d856dfc5d79b4f2b81883</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: How the funeral of Ratko Mladic is dividing a nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:849a69f8768a25e848033c6d73491546e56b272ba224cde226109969d173eaff</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890--47086bf0a8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the Serbian government leaves the decision about Ratko Mladic's funeral arrangements to his family, international pressure on the country is mounting. How do Serbs feel about the matter?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship in Svalbard to compensate Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da625dd8462a1e4086d112501e2215445f8ecdc11456312d229f65c26b06b64d</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005--08f506bc071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Norway have seized a Russian ship, the Professor Molchanov, on a court order sought and obtained by Naftogaz in Ukraine. Russia has protested the move, which stems from its refusal to pay Naftogaz damages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bea6e375cd3716b189ecf1ca2712cdb133bf64436933441b014a16219be91cc</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--2945f5b2dad4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a47b8dc832c72c1c8774d47d2aef6d9de435a7c84faf8bdd54382d8d1ab09101</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--4f4b3de05209.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37e4a02d3eb1b2a383bbbcdbb043e0c070f2d0c93ed1be3a6e4f3d34773d537f</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T00:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--a061a45930f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaad8694f4312b86abf4ea0cc8affc871c8ac6541c79dfdeeed410cb8d00394f</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--1b81c9b87e46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88d90a5db0e0ab923ffd37d6db27654625d2b4b26f35218c5fe7f4914fa6f984</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--165fe4759bb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
